 is indeed a festival of music and drama (opera, theatre). So answer: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.\n\nThus we need citation that Lilian Sukis performed at Salzburg Festival (sentence 6). And citation that Mozart was born in Salzburg? Not in provided evidence. We don't have evidence about Mozart. The evidence list does not include Mozart birth. So we cannot answer because we lack citation for Mozart's birthplace. Could there be other evidence? The evidence includes \"The National Peace Jubilee\", \"Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival\", \"Calcutta School of Music\", etc. None about Mozart. So we cannot provide citation for Mozart. Could there be another composer born in a town that hosts a festival that featured Lilian Sukis, with evidence present? Let's examine other festivals Lilian performed at: Bayreuth Festival (town Bayreuth). Famous composer born in Bayreuth? Richard Wagner was born in Leipzig, not Bayreuth. Not.\n\nFrankfurt Opera (city Frankfurt). Composer born in Frankfurt: perhaps \"Johann Wolfgang von Goethe\" (writer). Composer? \"Paul Hindemith\" was born in Frankfurt. He is a famous composer. Is there evidence of Hindemith birthplace? Not in given evidence.\n\nGraz (city Graz). Composer born in Graz: \"Johann Strauss II\"? He was born in Vienna. Not.\n\nHamburg State Opera (Hamburg). Composer born in Hamburg: \"Johannes Brahms\" was born in Hamburg. That is a famous composer. Do we have evidence of Brahms birthplace? Not in given evidence.\n\nVienna State Opera (Vienna). Composer born in Vienna: many, like Beethoven (born in Bonn), Mozart (born in Salzburg). Not.\n\nThus we lack evidence for any composer birthplace. The only evidence about a composer is in Calcutta School of Music: mentions Saint Saëns (Camille Saint-Saëns) but not birthplace. Also mentions Yehudi Menuhin, Isaac Stern, Mstislav Rostropovich, Ravi Shankar. Not birthplace.\n\nNational Peace Jubilee mentions Ole Bull (violinist) but not birthplace.\n\nCleveland Thyagaraja Festival mentions Tyagaraj